🏗️ System Architecture & Pipeline
Project Overview
This project is a Serverless IoT Room Analytics System designed for high-speed, low-latency monitoring. It integrates real-time AI-driven people counting via 5GHz Wi-Fi 6 and environmental sensing (CO2) via a modular Bluetooth sub-node.

📐 System Architecture
The system is divided into three main layers:

1. Sensor Edge Node (Peripheral)
MCU: ESP32 (Standard)

Sensor: SCD41 (Photoacoustic CO2 Sensor)

Function: Samples CO2, Temperature, and Humidity at 1-minute intervals.

Communication: Transmits data packets to the Main Gateway via Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) to maintain physical modularity and reduce interference.

2. AI Gateway Node (Central)
MCU: ESP32-C5 (Dual-band Wi-Fi 6 + RISC-V)

Camera: OV2640 (2MP) connected via PARLIO (Parallel IO) interface.

Connectivity: Utilizes the 5GHz band to bypass 2.4GHz congestion, ensuring a stable 15 FPS stream.

Role: Acts as the primary gateway. It receives BLE data from the Sensor Node and captures raw JPEG frames from the camera.

3. Cloud Processing & Logic Layer
Backend: FastAPI hosted on Hugging Face Spaces (Serverless).

AI Model: YOLOv8-tiny optimized for real-time human detection.

Database: Firebase Realtime Database.

Pipeline: 1.  Gateway POSTs raw JPEG buffers to the Cloud API.
2.  The API performs In-Memory Inference (Process-and-Delete) to detect people.
3.  A "Tripwire" logic counts entries/exits at the door region.
4.  Processed counts and CO2 telemetry are synced to Firebase.

🚀 Data Pipeline Flow
Capture: The ESP32-C5 captures JPEG frames at ~15 FPS with a resolution of 320x240 (QVGA) to balance detail and latency.

Transmission: Frames are transmitted over 5GHz Wi-Fi using a multipart/form-data POST request.

Inference: The Cloud-hosted Python script receives the image, converts it to an OpenCV object, and runs YOLOv8 detection.

Telemetry Merge: Every 60 seconds, the C5 injects the latest SCD41 sensor data (received via Bluetooth) into the metadata stream.

State Management: The final "Room Occupancy" and "Air Quality" states are pushed to Firebase, maintaining a total latency of <2 seconds.

🔋 Power Management
Battery: 5000mAh - 10000mAh LiPo (Lithium Polymer) flat pack.

Regulation: MT3608 DC-DC Boost Converter (Stable 5V output) and TP4056 for Type-C charging.

Efficiency: The system utilizes the 5GHz Wi-Fi 6 "Target Wake Time" (TWT) features of the ESP32-C5 (where applicable) to optimize power consumption during high-bandwidth streaming.

🛠️ Hardware Requirements
Main Controller: ESP32-C5 DevKit

Camera: OV2640 Module

Environment Sensor: SCD41

Power: 5000mAh LiPo Battery + TP4056 Charger
